1, <jats:italic>p</jats:italic> ∈ ℕ<jats:sup>*</jats:sup>, <jats:italic>m</jats:italic> ∈ <jats:italic>L<jats:sup>∞</jats:sup>\n                  </jats:italic> (Ω), <jats:italic>µ</jats:italic>{<jats:italic>x</jats:italic> ∈ Ω: <jats:italic>m</jats:italic>(<jats:italic>x</jats:italic>) &gt; 0} ≠ 0, and Δ<jats:sup>2</jats:sup>\n                  <jats:italic>\n                     <jats:sup>p</jats:sup>u</jats:italic> := Δ (Δ...(Δ<jats:italic>u</jats:italic>)), 2<jats:italic>p</jats:italic> times the operator Δ.</jats:p>\n               <jats:p>Using the Szulkin’s theorem, we establish the existence of at least one non decreasing sequence of nonnegative eigenvalues.</jats:p>	journal-article	1	10.2478/mjpaa-2022-0013	Walter de Gruyter GmbH	http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0	No publisher location	13	2351-8227	190	179	\N		http://dx.doi.org/10.2478/mjpaa-2022-0013	\N
