528	Archives of Medical and Biomedical Research	International Association of Medical and Biomedical Researchers (IAMBR) and the Society for Free Radical Research Africa (SFRR-Africa)	\N	https://www.ajol.info/index.php/ambr, https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=sw&sl=en&u=https://www.ajol.info/index.php/ambr&prev=search&pto=aue, https://www.ajol.info/index.php/ambr/about	f	f	f	1	f	16	f	nan	f	\N	t	f	t	f	t	t	'Archives of Medical and Biomedical Research' is a peer-reviewed, open-access journal that serves as a platform for disseminating original research and critical reviews in the field of medical and biomedical sciences. Its scope encompasses a wide array of disciplines, including but not limited to, clinical medicine, experimental medicine, molecular biology, genetics, immunology, pharmacology, pathology, and public health. The journal seeks to publish high-quality manuscripts that contribute significantly to the advancement of knowledge and understanding within these fields.\n\nKey themes explored within the journal include emerging technologies in medical diagnostics and treatment, disease pathogenesis and mechanisms, drug discovery and development, translational research, and public health interventions. The journal prioritizes manuscripts that address pressing medical challenges and propose innovative solutions for improving patient care and health outcomes. It also encourages research that explores the ethical and societal implications of biomedical advancements.\n\nThe target audience for 'Archives of Medical and Biomedical Research' comprises a diverse group of professionals, including researchers, clinicians, educators, students, and policymakers. The journal's open-access model ensures that its publications are accessible to a broad global readership, fostering knowledge exchange and collaboration across different institutions and geographic regions. This accessibility further contributes to the journal's impact by promoting the rapid dissemination of important findings and facilitating the translation of research into clinical practice.\n\n'Archives of Medical and Biomedical Research' plays a significant role in shaping the trajectory of medical and biomedical research by providing a platform for the publication of groundbreaking studies and fostering critical discourse within the scientific community. The journal's commitment to rigor, relevance, and accessibility ensures that its contributions have a lasting impact on the field, ultimately leading to improved patient care and health outcomes. \n	24	1	1	2	\N
