1032	South African Journal of Environmental Law and Policy - latest Issue	Juta and Company (Pty) Ltd (Juta's Law Journals)	\N	https://journals.co.za/journal/jlc.sajelp, https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=sw&sl=en&u=https://journals.co.za/journal/jlc.sajelp&prev=search&pto=aue, https://journals.co.za/journal/sajelp	f	\N	f	1	f	11	f	nan	f	\N	f	f	f	f	t	f	The South African Journal of Environmental Law and Policy (SAJELP) is a leading academic journal dedicated to fostering critical discourse and scholarship in the field of environmental law and policy within South Africa and beyond. It provides a platform for legal practitioners, academics, policymakers, and other stakeholders to engage in rigorous analysis of the complex legal and policy challenges related to environmental protection and sustainable development in the region.\n\nSAJELP focuses on a wide range of key themes, including, but not limited to, climate change law and policy, biodiversity conservation, environmental justice, water law and management, mining law and regulation, pollution control, land use planning, and the role of law in promoting sustainable development. The journal embraces interdisciplinary approaches, welcoming contributions from diverse fields such as law, environmental science, economics, sociology, and political science.\n\nThe target audience for SAJELP encompasses legal professionals, academics, policymakers, environmental activists, and other individuals involved in environmental governance. The journal aims to inform and influence legal practice, policy development, and public discourse on critical environmental issues facing South Africa and the wider African continent. \n\nSAJELP plays a crucial role in shaping the legal and policy landscape by providing a platform for cutting-edge research and analysis. Its publications have significantly contributed to the development of environmental law and policy in South Africa, influencing legal precedent, shaping policy debates, and raising awareness of critical environmental issues. The journal serves as a valuable resource for legal practitioners, policymakers, and researchers seeking to stay abreast of the latest developments and challenges in the field. \n	10	1	2	5	\N
1036	South African Journal of Information Management	AOSIS	\N	https://sajim.co.za/, https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=sw&sl=en&u=https://sajim.co.za/&prev=search&pto=aue, https://sajim.co.za/index.php/sajim/pages/view/journal-information	f	\N	t	23	f	14	f	nan	f	\N	f	f	t	t	t	f	The South African Journal of Information Management (SAJIM) is a scholarly publication dedicated to the advancement of information management knowledge and practice within the South African context. It serves as a platform for researchers, practitioners, and educators to share their insights on the evolving landscape of information management, exploring the challenges and opportunities arising from technological advancements, societal shifts, and global trends. The journal's scope encompasses a broad range of topics, including information systems, digital libraries, knowledge management, information retrieval, data analytics, information policy, information ethics, and information literacy.\n\nSAJIM prioritizes research that examines the intersection of information management with key societal and technological issues, particularly those relevant to the South African context. This includes topics such as the role of information in promoting social justice and equity, the impact of technology on information access and utilization, and the development of innovative information management solutions tailored to the specific needs of the South African population. The journal encourages interdisciplinary research, welcoming contributions from various fields, including computer science, library and information science, management science, and social sciences.\n\nThe journal's audience comprises a diverse group of stakeholders, including information professionals, academics, researchers, policymakers, and industry leaders interested in the latest developments and challenges in information management. It aims to facilitate knowledge sharing and collaboration among these stakeholders, fostering dialogue and debate on critical issues related to the effective management and utilization of information within South Africa and the broader African continent. SAJIM's impact extends beyond academia, as it provides valuable insights and recommendations for practitioners and policymakers seeking to implement effective information management strategies within their respective organizations and institutions.\n\nSAJIM contributes significantly to the body of knowledge on information management by publishing high-quality original research, review articles, case studies, and theoretical frameworks. Its rigorous peer-review process ensures the quality and relevance of published content, making it a valuable resource for researchers, educators, and practitioners seeking evidence-based insights and innovative approaches to information management challenges. The journal plays a critical role in shaping the future of information management in South Africa and beyond, fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and responsible utilization of information resources. \n	10	1	2	5	\N
1039	South African Journal of Philosophy = Suid-Afrikaanse Tydskrif vir Wysbegeerte	Taylor & Francis	\N	https://journals.co.za/journal/sajop, https://translate.google.com/translate?hl=sw&sl=en&u=https://journals.co.za/journal/sajop&prev=search&pto=aue, https://www.tandfonline.com/loi/rsph20	f	\N	f	1	f	21	f	nan	f	\N	f	f	f	f	t	f	The South African Journal of Philosophy, known in Afrikaans as Suid-Afrikaanse Tydskrif vir Wysbegeerte, stands as a distinguished platform for the dissemination of scholarly work in philosophy across the African continent. Its scope encompasses a broad spectrum of philosophical inquiry, embracing both traditional and contemporary themes. From metaphysics and epistemology to ethics, political philosophy, and aesthetics, the journal welcomes diverse perspectives and approaches, fostering a vibrant intellectual landscape. \n\nKey themes explored within the journal often reflect the unique cultural and societal contexts of South Africa, drawing on its rich history and diverse perspectives. Articles delve into issues of social justice, race, colonialism, and the legacy of apartheid, offering critical analyses and innovative solutions. Additionally, the journal engages with global philosophical debates, providing a platform for South African scholars to contribute to international discourse.\n\nThe audience for the South African Journal of Philosophy comprises a diverse group of scholars, including academics, researchers, and students specializing in philosophy and related fields. Its readership extends beyond South Africa, encompassing individuals with an interest in African philosophy and the unique challenges and opportunities facing the continent. By fostering communication and knowledge sharing, the journal plays a vital role in shaping the intellectual landscape of the region.\n\nThe South African Journal of Philosophy has a significant impact on the development of philosophical scholarship within South Africa and beyond. Its publications stimulate dialogue and critical engagement, contributing to the advancement of philosophical thought and its application to contemporary issues. Through its commitment to rigorous scholarship and inclusive representation, the journal continues to provide a platform for groundbreaking research and insightful discussions, shaping the philosophical landscape of the continent and enriching global discourse. \n	10	1	2	5	\N
1523	African Journal of Infectious Diseases Research	International Scholars Journal 	2756-3340	https://internationalscholarsjournals.org/journal/ajidd/abou	f	f	\N	1	f	26	f	nan	f	\N	\N	f	t	f	t	f	The African Journal of Infectious Diseases Research is a peer-reviewed, open-access journal dedicated to disseminating high-quality research on the burden, prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of infectious diseases in Africa. Its scope encompasses a wide range of topics, including emerging and re-emerging infectious diseases, tropical diseases, HIV/AIDS, tuberculosis, malaria, and neglected tropical diseases. The journal welcomes original research articles, review articles, case reports, and short communications.\n\nThe journal's key themes are rooted in the unique challenges and complexities of infectious disease control and management in the African context. These include the impact of poverty, social determinants of health, and limited access to healthcare on disease transmission and outcomes. The journal also focuses on the development and implementation of innovative approaches to prevention, diagnosis, and treatment, including the use of new technologies, community-based interventions, and participatory research.\n\nThe journal's target audience includes researchers, clinicians, public health practitioners, policymakers, and other stakeholders involved in infectious disease control and management in Africa. The journal aims to provide a platform for the dissemination of research findings and best practices, promoting collaboration and knowledge sharing among the African scientific community and beyond.\n\nThe African Journal of Infectious Diseases Research has established a strong reputation for its rigorous peer-review process and its commitment to publishing high-quality, impactful research. The journal plays a crucial role in advancing understanding of infectious diseases in Africa, informing policy decisions, and contributing to the development of effective interventions. The journal's articles have been cited extensively, and its research has been featured in prominent international media outlets. The journal's impact is further amplified by its open-access model, which ensures that research findings are freely available to a global audience. \n	7	1	\N	149	\N
